module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.CohenMacaulaySlice.GermsToSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Unramified.AtPointCriteria
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.LocalRing.MinimalGenerators
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.RegularLocalRing.Basic

/-!
# The slicing sequence of an unramified morphism at a regular point

Let `q : V ⟶ U` be a morphism of schemes locally of finite type which is **unramified** at a
point `v` of `V`, and suppose the local ring `𝒪_{V, v}` is **regular**. This file produces the
sequence the chart construction of **Stacks 06N3** slices by:

> `f₁, …, f_d ∈ 𝔪_u ⊆ 𝒪_{U, u}`, where `u = q v`, whose images in `𝒪_{V, v}` form a regular
> sequence **generating** `𝔪_v`.

Unramifiedness at `v` enters only through the first clause by which **Stacks 02GF** recognizes
it, `φ(𝔪_u) 𝒪_{V, v} = 𝔪_v`; the other clause, finite separability of `κ(v)/κ(u)`, is not used.
Granted that equality, `𝔪_v` is generated by the images of `(𝔪_v).spanFinrank` elements of `𝔪_u`
(`IsLocalRing.exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_ofList_map_eq_maximalIdeal`), and a minimal generating
family of the maximal ideal of a regular local ring is a regular sequence (**Stacks 00NQ**).

That the sequence **generates** `𝔪_v`, and does not merely cut `𝒪_{V, v}` down to dimension
zero, is the whole point: it is what makes the local ring of the slice the residue field `κ(v)`
and hence the slice unramified over the base, by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.isField_fiberStalk_comp_of_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_fiberStalk`. A
zero-dimensional local ring need not be a field, so the quasi-finiteness datum of **Stacks 06LC**
cannot be upgraded to this one.

The second result realizes the germs `f_i` as honest regular functions on an **affine open**
`W ⊆ U` containing `u`, by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq`; that is the
source's first shrinking of `U`, after which the `f_i` are global functions on the chart and the
slicing lemmas can be applied to them.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry`
  `.exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt`:
  the slicing sequence, as germs in `𝒪_{U, u}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt`:
  the same sequence read as regular functions on an affine open of `U` containing `u`.

## Implementation notes

The sister statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_mem_maximalIdeal_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_fiberStalk_of_smooth`
produces the same kind of sequence at the local ring of the **scheme-theoretic fibre** of a
smooth morphism, and takes the ideal equality as a hypothesis because the morphism out of a
fibre need not be locally of finite type, which puts Stacks 02GF out of reach at the composite.
Here the morphism is `q` itself, so the ideal equality is *derived* from unramifiedness at `v`
rather than assumed: it is the seventh entry of `AlgebraicGeometry.unramifiedAt_tfae`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is claimed. Stacks 02GF is registered on
`AlgebraicGeometry.unramifiedAt_tfae` and Stacks 00NQ on
`IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay`;
this is a step of the proof of **Stacks 06N3**, which is no tag of its own.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 00NQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00NQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02GF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02GF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06N3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06N3)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **The slicing sequence of the chart construction of Stacks 06N3.** Let `q : V ⟶ U` be a
morphism of schemes locally of finite type, let `v` be a point of `V` at which `q` is
**unramified**, and suppose `𝒪_{V, v}` is a regular local ring. Then there are
`d = (𝔪_v).spanFinrank` elements of the maximal ideal of `𝒪_{U, q v}` whose images in
`𝒪_{V, v}` form a regular sequence **generating** `𝔪_v`.

This is the source's *"choose `f₁, …, f_d ∈ 𝒪_{U, u}` whose images give a basis of
`𝔪_v/𝔪_v²`; these form a regular sequence since `𝒪_{V, v}` is regular"*. Unramifiedness is used
only for `φ(𝔪_u) 𝒪_{V, v} = 𝔪_v`, the seventh entry of `AlgebraicGeometry.unramifiedAt_tfae`
(**Stacks 02GF**); the minimal generating family inside `𝔪_u` is
`IsLocalRing.exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_ofList_map_eq_maximalIdeal`, and its regularity is
**Stacks 00NQ**. -/
theorem exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt
    {V U : Scheme.{u}} (q : V ⟶ U) [LocallyOfFiniteType q] (v : V)
    (hq : UnramifiedAt q v) (hreg : IsRegularLocalRing (V.presheaf.stalk v)) :
    ∃ t : Fin (maximalIdeal (V.presheaf.stalk v)).spanFinrank → U.presheaf.stalk (q v),
      (∀ i, t i ∈ maximalIdeal (U.presheaf.stalk (q v))) ∧
        RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (V.presheaf.stalk v)
            (List.ofFn fun i => (q.stalkMap v).hom (t i)) ∧
          Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn fun i => (q.stalkMap v).hom (t i)) =
            maximalIdeal (V.presheaf.stalk v) := by
  have := hreg
  -- Stacks 02GF: unramifiedness at `v` makes `𝔪_u` generate `𝔪_v`
  have hall := ((unramifiedAt_tfae q v).out 1 7).mp hq
  have hmap : Ideal.map (q.stalkMap v).hom (maximalIdeal (U.presheaf.stalk (q v))) =
      maximalIdeal (V.presheaf.stalk v) := hall.1
  -- the minimal generating family of `𝔪_v` drawn from `𝔪_u`
  obtain ⟨t, htmem, htspan⟩ :=
    IsLocalRing.exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_ofList_map_eq_maximalIdeal (q.stalkMap v).hom hmap
  -- Stacks 00NQ: a minimal generating family of the maximal ideal of a regular local ring is a
  -- regular sequence
  exact ⟨t, htmem,
    (IsRegularLocalRing.isRegular_and_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_and_isMaximalCohenMacaulay
      (V.presheaf.stalk v)).1 _ htspan (by rw [List.length_ofFn]) |>.1, htspan⟩

/-- **The slicing sequence of Stacks 06N3 as regular functions on an affine open.** In the
situation of
`AlgebraicGeometry`
`.exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt`
the sequence can be taken to consist of the germs at `u = q v` of regular functions on an affine
open `W ⊆ U` containing `u`.

This is the source's first shrinking of `U`: once `U` is replaced by `W`, the `f_i` are global
functions on the chart, which is the form in which the slicing lemmas consume them. Passing from
germs to sections is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq`. -/
theorem exists_isAffineOpen_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt
    {V U : Scheme.{u}} (q : V ⟶ U) [LocallyOfFiniteType q] (v : V)
    (hq : UnramifiedAt q v) (hreg : IsRegularLocalRing (V.presheaf.stalk v)) :
    ∃ (d : ℕ) (W : U.Opens) (hW : q v ∈ W), IsAffineOpen W ∧
      ∃ g : Fin d → Γ(U, W),
        (∀ i, U.presheaf.germ W (q v) hW (g i) ∈
          maximalIdeal (U.presheaf.stalk (q v))) ∧
          RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (V.presheaf.stalk v)
              (List.ofFn fun i =>
                (q.stalkMap v).hom (U.presheaf.germ W (q v) hW (g i))) ∧
            Ideal.ofList (List.ofFn fun i =>
                (q.stalkMap v).hom (U.presheaf.germ W (q v) hW (g i))) =
              maximalIdeal (V.presheaf.stalk v) := by
  obtain ⟨t, htmem, htreg, htspan⟩ :=
    exists_fn_mem_maximalIdeal_isRegular_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal_stalk_of_unramifiedAt q v hq hreg
  obtain ⟨W, hW, hWaff, g, hg⟩ := Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_germ_eq (q v) t
  refine ⟨_, W, hW, hWaff, g, fun i => ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [hg i]; exact htmem i
  · simpa only [hg] using htreg
  · simpa only [hg] using htspan

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
